				Type Casting
Unifying Data Type
	• different data types are automatically converted into a unifying type
	• the unifying type is based on the following level of precedence
		1. double 		accurate to fifteen decimal places
		2. float 		accurate to seven decimal places
		3. long 		very large whole number
		4. int 			–2,147,483,648 to 2,147,483,647
		5. short 		-32,768 to 32,767
		6. byte 		-128 to 127

	• the double data type has the highest level of precedence
		o any other data type can be assigned to a double
		o thus:
			double digit = 1.7;
			int number = 1;
			digit = number; // automatic conversion
		o but:
			number = digit; //error
			 number is an integer
			 integer has a lower level of precedence than a double

Type Casting
	• overriding the unifying type
	• place the desired type in parentheses followed by the variable to be cast
			double digit = 1.7;
			int number = (int) digit; //type cast
			print(number) //prints 1
		o truncates decimal part of 1.7 to create 1
		o integers do not have a decimal
